ide. #coffesoftware #jamesward","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TdwUN1dvHCg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/letting-the-model-decide-coffesoftware-jamesward-t4vbdmywm","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TdwUN1dvHCg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T20:46:58.000Z"},{"id":"96gkeUR1g","title":"Agent skills. #jamesward #coffesoftware","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=32CsWaK09iY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/agent-skills-jamesward-coffesoftware-96gkeur1g","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/32CsWaK09iY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T20:45:29.000Z"},{"id":"ELnAr8YuH","title":"the why with #jenniferreif #neo4j #coffesoftware","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HjRzEzvNuxg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-why-with-jenniferreif-neo4j-coffesoftware-elnar8yuh","summary":"Jennifer Reif from Neo4j discusses how the industry has moved beyond RAG toward agentic AI, MCP, and memory, and how graph databases naturally fit this evolution. She introduces the concept of a 'context graph' \u2014 using graphs to document business decisions, the reasoning behind processes, and chat memory, so AI agents can share context, communicate, and make better-informed decisions over time.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/HjRzEzvNuxg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T22:57:49.000Z"},{"id":"QBvgJn1cC","title":"making connections with  #jenniferreif #neo4j #coffesoftware","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AkKRYwSvqKY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/making-connections-with-jenniferreif-neo4j-coffesoftware-qbvgjn1cc","summary":"A discussion using the Panama Papers investigation as an example to illustrate the power of graph databases like Neo4j. The key insight is that graph databases allow connections between data points to emerge organically after ingestion, whereas SQL databases require relationships to be defined upfront \u2014 making graph databases particularly valuable for exploratory analysis of large, complex datasets.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/AkKRYwSvqKY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T22:53:13.000Z"},{"id":"J3mLQeKJO","title":"accidentally recreating sypher with #jenniferreif #neo4j #coffesoftware","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2VXAaPLcLKQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/accidentally-recreating-sypher-with-jenniferreif-neo4j-coffesoftware-j3mlqekjo","summary":"A casual conversation snippet exploring how Cypher, Neo4j's graph query language, is so intuitive that developers might naturally reinvent it on their own when trying to describe graph relationships using simple arrow notation.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2VXAaPLcLKQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T22:48:20.000Z"},{"id":"pI8SGbo1J","title":"boxes and lines with @neo4j  @JMHReif #coffeesoftware","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VAG8s2aQK60","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/boxes-and-lines-with-neo4j-jmhreif-coffeesoftware-pi8sgbo1j","summary":"A conversational snippet discussing the intuitive nature of graph databases, specifically Neo4j. The speakers highlight how humans naturally think in graphs (boxes and lines/circles and arrows) and how graph databases like Neo4j allow storing and querying data exactly as it's mentally modeled, eliminating the object-relational impedance mismatch.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/VAG8s2aQK60/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T22:45:42.000Z"},{"id":"HLVWPmdHB","title":"getting started with @neo4j #coffeesoftware","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q4TwN3hoATE","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/getting-started-with-neo4j-coffeesoftware-hlvwpmdhb","summary":"A brief walkthrough of spinning up a free Neo4j instance, loading the classic movies example dataset from the Neo4j GitHub graph examples repository, and running Cypher queries to create constraints, indexes, and nodes for movies, actors, and persons.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/q4TwN3hoATE/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T21:28:24.000Z"},{"id":"UK3HXFvJj","title":"JobRunr, ClawRunr, and more with Ronald Dehuysser","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RbkpxQWvGms","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/jobrunr-clawrunr-and-more-with-ronald-dehuysser-uk3hxfvjj","summary":"Ronald Dehuysser, creator of JobRunr, discusses two projects at Spring IO Barcelona. ClawRunr (formerly JavaClaw) is an open-source Java-based personal AI assistant built on Spring AI and JobRunr, inspired by Open Claude. It uses MCP servers to monitor emails and WhatsApp messages, schedule recurring agent tasks, and draft responses. It supports multiple AI models (Claude, Gemini, Ollama) and uses Spring AI's dynamic tool search to reduce token costs. JobRunr also recently launched carbon-aware job scheduling for the US, using Electricity Maps data to run jobs during periods of low-carbon electricity, with a visual dashboard to validate scheduling decisions.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/RbkpxQWvGms/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-15T21:15:01.000Z"},{"id":"mi9aflCXu","title":"Secure by Design: How Hardened Images Make Your Java Services Bullet-Proof","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Zfo_HAQOk0","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/secure-by-design-how-hardened-images-make-your-java-services-bullet-proof-mi9aflcxu","summary":"Container images are a major but often overlooked security surface. The average container image contains 600+ vulnerabilities, and 44% of Java services contain known exploited CVEs. Hardened container images \u2014 offered by vendors like BellSoft (Liberica JDK on Alpaquita Linux), Chainguard, and Docker Hub \u2014 address this by providing minimalistic, distroless-friendly base images with low-to-zero CVEs and continuous vendor-managed patching. Key features include no package manager, non-root defaults, software bill of materials (SBOM), and digital signatures for supply chain integrity. Migration is as simple as changing the FROM line in a Dockerfile. The talk also covers Docker multi-stage builds (JDK for build, JRE for run), Cloud Native Buildpacks as a more secure alternative to Dockerfiles (with rebasing support), SLSA compliance levels, and Cosign for image signature verification. BellSoft's hardened images are free to use, with commercial support available for SLA-backed patching.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/9Zfo_HAQOk0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-10T01:13:45.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["jbhuang0604","nopriorspodcast","gdcfestivalofgaming","watchtowr-labs","devoxx"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"jbhuang0604","handle":"jbhuang0604","name":"Jia-Bin Huang","is_squad":false,"x":-2.0482,"y":-7.9956,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":47,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--8hwFrfWM--/f_auto,q_auto/v1776585907/logos/jbhuang0604","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":21.479692,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.010638,"avg_read_time":10.978723,"tag_diversity":0.574468},"top_tags_preview":[["computer-vision",17],["diffusion-models",13],["deep-learning",11]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-8.9559,-8.4706],"cadence_depth":[-4.6912,6.9559],"hype_variety":[1.6029,-3.4118],"title_style":[1.25,-5.5294]}},{"id":"nopriorspodcast","handle":"nopriorspodcast","name":"No Priors: AI, Machine Learning, Tech, & Startups","is_squad":false,"x":-1.8916,"y":-7.6556,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":93,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--Hj2kMkm_--/f_auto,q_auto/v1772391934/logos/nopriorspodcast","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":9.9